<Project>
  <!--
    Suppress low-priority code analysis and other warnings to clean up the build output.
    Keep meaningful warnings like CA1716 (keyword conflicts) visible for code quality.

    Code analysis (CA*) suppressions:
    CA2000 (92): Dispose objects before losing scope — mostly in test projects.
    CA2234 (48): Pass System.Uri objects instead of strings — style preference.
    CA1054 (12): URI-based strings should be System.Uri — same as CA2234.
    CA1307 (6):  Specify StringComparison — mostly in test code.
    CA1308 (6):  Normalize strings to uppercase — style issue in tests.
    CA1844 (4):  Provide memory-based overrides of async methods — not broadly applicable.
    CA5399 (4):  HttpClient instances should be reused — mostly test code.
    CA1506 (2):  Avoid excessive class coupling — architectural limitation.
    CA1032 (4):  Add constructor overloads — low-priority exception constructors.
    CA1034 (4):  Nested types — intentional design.
    CA1055 (4):  URI return types — style preference.
    CA1068 (2):  CancellationToken parameters — not mandatory in internal code.
    CA1825 (2):  Avoid zero-length array allocations — rare edge case.
    CA1502 (4):  Avoid excessive complexity — code review item, not breaking.
    CA1024 (4):  Use properties instead of get_ methods — design choice.
    CA1305 (16): Specify IFormatProvider — mostly in tests.
    CA1849 (12): Call async methods from async code — test code and edge cases.
    CA2016 (12): Forward parameter to disposable — legitimate call patterns.

    Naming/documentation (CS*, xUnit*):
    CS1591 (36): Missing XML documentation — optional for internal code.
    CS8605 (6):  Nullability warnings in unobserved expressions — low impact.
    CS8600 (2):  Null reference assignment — handled by developers.
    xUnit1051 (22): Test naming — project convention.

    NuGet (NU*):
    NU1701: Library compiled with newer .NET version — expected.
    NU1603: Dependency version mismatch — acceptable resolution.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA2000;CA2234;CA1054;CA1307;CA1308;CA1844;CA5399;CA1506;CA1032;CA1034;CA1055;CA1068;CA1825;CA1502;CA1024;CA1305;CA1849;CA2016;CS1591;CS8605;CS8600;NU1701;NU1603;VSTHRD200;CS8604</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
